id: pm-github-rap0
title: Root CI runs skip the read-only-directory comment-sync fixtures visibly instead of failing them
description: "The review-round1 new Function test removal moved the chmod 0o555/finally cleanup of the comment-sync write-failure fixture into the exported withReadOnlyDirectory test helper. Root ignores directory write permissions, so under a root CI runner the helper applies no read-only mode, the fixture write succeeds, and the per-comment write-failure assertions in the comment-sync coverage test fail. Review round 3 guarded the equivalent import-lock fixtures with a visible node:test root skip (CodeRabbit 4198811222); the same non-root-only skip should cover this helper-based fixture so a root run skips visibly instead of failing."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,root,tests
created_at: "2026-10-06T18:29:11.654Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T12:39:24.056Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T08:33:51.527Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T08:33:51.527Z"
author: pi-gh-cr3b
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-06T18:29:15.904Z",pi-gh-cr3b,"Discovered during review round 3 (CodeRabbit 4198811228): replacing the new Function source-slicing test exposed that the coverage-remainder comment-sync write-failure fixture inherits the same root-sensitivity as the import-lock permission fixtures, but the review only authorized guarding import-lock.test.ts this round. Left as a follow-up so a root CI runner skips it visibly instead of failing the suite."
close_reason: "Resolved on PR #108 by the orchestrator: all three read-only-directory comment-sync fixtures in test/coverage-remainder.test.ts (per-comment add failure gated and ungated, contended lock plus per-comment failure) now use a visible nonRootOnly skip when the suite runs as root, matching test/import-lock.test.ts; non-root CI still runs them (verified 3/3 pass)."
body: ""
